From dfeae4d21233111ef3d5da207ee24a86b39349a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:05:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2268/2271] dt-bindings: display: vop2: Add the RK3588 DCLK
 sources and their parents

On RK3588 the pixel clock of video ports 0-2 is a mux between the HDMI
PHY PLLs and a CRU divider (dclk_vopN_src); video port 3 has the CRU
divider only. Each divider can run from GPLL, CPLL, AUPLL or the video
PLL (V0PLL). The fixed PLLs only give integer fractions of their rates,
and V0PLL is the one clock that can be set for a pixel clock, but all
video ports share it.

To decide which parent each video port uses, and run every video port
that shares V0PLL from one rate, the display controller has to select
the parent of each divider itself. Describe the dividers of video ports
0-2 (dclk_src_vp0..2) and the fixed parents (pll_gpll, pll_cpll,
pll_aupll) as optional clocks after the video PLL.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
